descript     = "yt-dlp Web UI is a self-hosted web interface and RPC server for yt-dlp, the popular video and audio downloader. Paste a video or playlist link, optionally choose a format, and your NAS downloads it in the background with live progress, a download queue and a log console. A built-in file browser lists, previews and serves the finished files to any device on your LAN. This package bundles the yt-dlp runtime (official Python zipapp) and the lightweight quickjs JavaScript engine that yt-dlp needs for YouTube; ffmpeg is taken from the TOS system packages. The app opens in a new browser tab from the TOS desktop. The backend listens on loopback only, so no extra port is exposed and all traffic goes through the TOS web server. It runs as a dedicated unprivileged user inside a hardened systemd sandbox. No separate account is required: access is protected by your TOS login."
release_note = "Built from the upstream yt-dlp-web-ui 4.0.0 source code (static Go binary with the web frontend embedded; public CI build with an auditable source chain). Bundles yt-dlp 2026.08.19 (official Python zipapp) and quickjs-ng 0.17.0 (compiled from source) so YouTube downloads work out of the box; ffmpeg is used from the TOS system packages. Downloads, the queue database and logs live in /var/lib/ytdlpwebui. Configuration lives in /usr/local/ytdlpwebui/config.yml and /usr/local/ytdlpwebui/ytdlpwebui.env; restart the service after editing."
important    = "No default password is needed: open the app from the TOS desktop and you are authenticated by your TOS account. Downloads are stored in /var/lib/ytdlpwebui/downloads by default; retrieve them with the built-in file browser, or set another directory in /usr/local/ytdlpwebui/ytdlpwebui.env and restart the service. 'apt remove' keeps all data in /var/lib/ytdlpwebui; 'apt purge' deletes everything. The system ffmpeg package is required to merge separate video and audio streams. Upstream license: GPL-3.0."

